{
  "dom_id": "step-187406",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying Situations When the CLT for Proportions is Appropriate",
  "problem": "For which of the following situations can the distribution of the sample proportion $\\widehat{\\,p}$ be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\widehat{\\,p} \\sim N\\left(p,\\dfrac{p(1-p)}{n}\\right),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the population proportion?\n\nI. A sample of $120$ apricots from a population of $20\\,000$, where $75\\%$ of the apricots weigh more than $50$ g.\n\nII. A sample of $25$ gym members from a population containing $200$ members, where $80\\%$ of the gym's members work out for more than $100$ minutes each visit.\n\nIII. A sample of $45$ flights in an airport, given that $90\\%$ of flights arrive on time. You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.",
  "worked_solution": "Given a population in which a proportion $p$ of the population has a particular characteristic, the sampling distribution of the sample proportion $\\widehat{\\,p}$ can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\widehat{\\,p} \\sim N\\left( p, \\dfrac{p(1-p)}{n} \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $n\\leq 5\\% \\cdot N$ (the sample size is less than (or equal to) $5\\%$ of the population size),\n\n- $np > 5$ (more than $5$ sample elements have the characteristic), and\n\n- $n(1-p) > 5$ (more than $5$ sample elements do not have the characteristic).\n\nLet's now examine each situation.\n\n- In situation I, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =120 \\\\  & \\le 5%\\cdot N \\\\  & =0.05\\cdot 20\\,000 \\\\  & =1\\,000\\,✓ \\\\ np & =120(0.75) \\\\  & =90 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =120(1-0.75) \\\\  & =30 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can approximate the distribution of $\\widehat{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\n- In situation II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =25, \\\\ 5%\\cdot N & =0.05\\cdot 200 \\\\  & =10 \\\\  & <25.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the sample size is more than $5\\%$ of the population size, we *cannot* approximate the distribution of $\\widehat{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\n- In situation III, we're given that the population is significantly larger than the sample size in each case. Therefore, we may assume that the first condition is satisfied. \n\nFor the other conditions, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =45(0.9) \\\\  & =40.5 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =45(1-0.9) \\\\  & =4.5 \\\\  & ≯5.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $n(1-p) \\ngtr 5,$ we *cannot* approximate the distribution of $\\widehat{\\,p}$ using the given model.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-187406\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"187406\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"15151\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-187406\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-3\">Identifying Situations When the CLT for Proportions is Appropriate</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"187406\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: